  "raw_text": "72\n\nKwah damni dusa\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nfig tree\n \n/ higuera\n\nOliv dusa\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nolive tree\n \n/ olivo\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-02/19\n):\n \nOliv dusa maprika lilka ba\n \n–\n \nThe illustration of the olive tree\n \n/ La ilustración del olivo)\n\nDusa\n \n(n/s-2)\n \n–\n \nbone\n \n/ hueso\n\n(Construct:\n \nDusi\n \n–\n \nmy bone\n \n/ mi hueso;\n \nDusam\n \n–\n \nyour bone\n \n/ tu hueso;\n \nAi dusa\n \n–\n \nhis/her/its/their bone\n \n/ su hueso\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nbh48\n):\n \n(Gâd) wîna bara dusa sin apu sa\n \n–\n \n(God) does not have flesh and bone.\n \n(Note that\n \nbone\n \nis used instead of\n \nblood\n.) /\n(Dios) no tiene carne ni hueso.\n \n(\nNota\n \nse usa\n \nhueso\n \nen lugar de\n \nsangre\n.\n)\n)\n\nDutki\n \n(adj,adv)\n \n–\n \nstrong, strongly, firm, firmly, tight, tightly\n \n/ fuerte, firme, apretado\n\nDutki alkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto hold tightly, to hold strongly\n \n/ sostener con fuerza, mantener fuerte\n\nDutki bapi buaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto endure in a firm and strong way, to stand up to in a firm and strong way, to stand up for\nin a firm and strong way\n \n/\n \naguantar de manera firme y fuerte, resistir de manera firme y fuerte, defender de\nmanera firme y fuerte\n\nDutki daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto make strong, to strengthen, to tighten\n \n/ hacer fuerte, fortalecer, apretar\n\nDutki kaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto be strong\n \n/ ser fuerte\n\nDutki takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become strong, to become firm, to become tight\n \n/ volverse fuerte, hacerse firme, apretarse\n\nDwarka\n \n–\n \nconstruct of/de:\n \nDuri\n\nElepant\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nelephant\n \n/ elefante\n\nEmus\n \n(\ndb,dba\n;\n \nEmos\n-\nbw\n;\n \nAmós\n-\ndbta\n)\n \n–\n \nAmos\n \n(Bible book)\n \n/ Am\nó\ns (\nlibro bíblico)\n\nEpesus\n \n(\ndb\n,dba\n;\n \nEfesus Nanira\n-\ndbta,lrw\n)\n \n–\n \nEphesians\n \n(Bible book)\n \n/ Efesios\n \n(libro bíblico)\n\nEsdras\n \n(\ndb\n,dbta\n;\n \nEsra\n-\nbw\n)\n \n–\n \nEz\nr\na\n \n(Bible book)\n \n/ Esdras\n \n(libro bíblico)\n\nEsia\n \n–\n \nAsia\n \n/ Asia\n\nEster\n \n(\ndb,dba\n,\ndbta\n,bw\n)\n \n–\n \nEsther\n \n(Bible book)\n \n/ Ester\n \n(libro bíblico)\n\nEt\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nIt\n\nEur\nu\np\n \n–\n \nEurope\n \n/ Europa\n\nFrancia\n \n–\n \nFrance\n \n/ Francia\n\nGabamint\n \n(\nbh,bm,fy,gf,fg,km,kt,ll,lv,sn,sp,t36\n;\n \nGabament\n-\ndict\n,\ndictu\n; Gabamit\n-\nmy\n;\n \nGabamint\n-\ndictu\n-\nalt\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n\ngovernment\n \n/ gobierno\n\nGabamint suliarka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ngovernment employee\n \n/ empleado del gobierno\n\nG\nâ\nd ra mayunaia warkka daukaia apia\n \ngabamint nani\n \n–\n \ngovernments\n \nthat\n \nban the work of worshipping God\n \n/ los\n\ngobiernos\n \nque\n \nprohíben el trabajo de adorar a Dios\n\nHeven gabamintka\n \n(\nkt,bh,gf\n)\n \n–\n \nheavenly government\n \n/ gobierno celestial\n\nTasba gabamintka\n \n–\n \nhuman\n \ngovernment\n \n/ gobierno\n \nhumano\n\nGâd\n \n(Gad)\n \n(\ndb,dba\n, ...;\n \nGod\n-bw,lrw,sln\n;\n \nGad\n,\nGod\n-dbta\n;\n \nGod\n,\nGad\n-dictu\n;\n \nGad\n,\nGod\n-dict\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ngod\n \n/ dios\n\n(Construct:\n \nGâdki\n;\n \nGâdkam\n;\n \nGâdka\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb33\n):\n \nMan uplikam nani ba, upliki nani kabia, man Gâdkam ba Gâdki kabia\n \n–\n \nYour people will be my people and your God\nwill be my God\n \n/ Tu pueblo será mi pueblo y tu Dios será mi Dios)\n\nGâdkas\n \n–\n \ngodless, without God\n \n/ sin Dios\n\nGâd king aimakaia raitka\n \n–\n \nGod’s right to rule, God’s sovereignty\n \n/ derecho de Dios a gobernar, soberanía de\nDios\n\nGâd Kingka lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nGod’s Kingdom\n \n/ El reino de dios\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nGâd\n \nK\ningka lâka ba dia daukbia?\n \n–\n \nWhat will God's kingdom do?\n \n/ ¿Qué hará el reino de Dios?)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ntkl\n):\n \nGâd Kingka lâka sturka yamni smalkanka ba tnata yua nani sainka markka tânka tara bri ba kum sa\n \n–\n \nThe\n\npreaching of the good news is an important feature of the sign of the last days\n \n/ La predicación de las buenas noticias del\n\nReino de Dios es una característica importante de la señal de los\n \nú\nltimos d\ní\nas\n)\n\nG\nâ\nd Kumira Yuhmpa\n \n(\nbh\n;\n \nKumira asla yuhmpa ba l\nâ\nka\n-\ndict\n)\n \n–\n \nt\nrinity\n \n/\n \nt\nrinidad\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nbh152\n):\n \nG\nâ\nd Kumira\n \nYuhmpa mayuni\n \nbangwisa\n \n–\n \nThey worship the trinity\n \n/ Ellos adoran a la trinidad\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nbh202\n):\n \n“G\nâ\nd Kumira Yuhmpa” bila aisanka ba, Baibil ra aima kumi sin takras.\n \n–\n \nThe expression “God three persons\n\nin one” (Trinity) does not occur once in the Bible.\n \n/ La expresión \"Dios tres personas en una\" (Trinidad) no aparece\n \nni\n \nuna\n\nvez en la Biblia.\n)\n\nGâd kuninkira\n \n–\n \nfalse god\n \n/ dios falso\n\nGâd lilia pali ba\n \n(\ntnm\n-\n1Tim 1:11\n)\n \n–\n \nthe happy God\n \n/ el Dios feliz\n\nGâd Warkka Dauki\n \n–\n \nOur Kingdom Ministry\n \n/ Nuestro Ministerio del Reino",
